MID_SE_Bon_Tob_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_C_001: Best to send our cavalry this way to break through\nthe enemy line. Though given the terrain...
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_C_002: That's not the Bona I know.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_C_003: Tobias? What makes you say that?
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_C_004: I've seen you in here a lot, mumbling to yourself\nabout the best tactics to use.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_C_005: Time was, that stuff got settled over shouting\nmatches with King Sergio.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_C_006: They weren't shouting matches. We would debate.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_C_007: But I do miss those days. King Sergio was a young\nman then, and I was an untested recruit.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_C_008: Looking back, I cannot believe I had the gall to\noffer advice to such a great man.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_C_009: Hehehe. I can. You were both young hotheads.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_C_010: Despite our clashes at war councils, we always\ntrusted each other's intuition on the battlefield.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_C_011: It may be those "shouting matches," as you put it,\nwhich built that trust.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_C_012: Yeah, I get that. When you fight with someone,\nyou end up knowing exactly where they stand.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_C_013: You ever tried getting into it with the boss like\nyou did with King Sergio?
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_C_014: No, and nor will I. There's no use in intentionally\nprovoking arguments.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_C_015: Queen Theodora already has full faith in my tactics.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_C_016: Hm! Is that not why they call me Her Majesty's\nright arm?
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_C_017: Yeah, absolutely.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_C_018: Besides, the boss is a softy. She wouldn't scrap with\nyou even if you begged.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_C_019: Tobias, do you ever intend to call Her Majesty\nby her proper title?
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_C_020: Sorry, but she'll always be the boss to me!\nBaw haw haw!
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_C_021: Oh dear. I was afraid of that.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_B_001: I believe that's all the arrows. Take them back\nto base!
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_B_002: Hey, Bona! You up for some postbattle mead?\nOr we could scrounge up some wine!
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_B_003: No, thank you. I am not the hedonist you insist\non being, even at your age.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_B_004: You are so set in your ways that you still won't call\nme by my proper name. It's a lost cause.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_B_005: Huh. Speaking of which, I can't even remember\nwhen I started calling you Bona.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_B_006: You always have, I believe. Don't you recall us\nfighting a duel over it?
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_B_007: We did?
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_B_008: Some time before Queen Theodora was born.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_B_009: I approached you to admonish you for your\noutrageous behavior in camp.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_B_010: Do you recall your answer?
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_B_011: Nope. What'd I say?
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_B_012: You said, quote, "Who the hell are you?"
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_B_013: Apparently not remembering we had met many\ntimes as vassals in King Sergio's war councils.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_B_014: Ohhh, I remember this now! You turned red as\na stewed tomato!
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_B_015: You are insufferable. Anyone would lose their temper\nwhen faced with such disrespect!
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_B_016: Kumos tried to hold you back, but you came at me\nanyway, dragging him along.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_B_017: You said, "Now see here!" and we had it out,\nright on the spot!
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_B_018: Neither of us won, but I think you and me\nunderstood each other better after that.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_B_019: You learned my name, at the very least. Though you\nclaimed it was too long.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_B_020: Baw haw haw! I only shorten my friends' names.\nI liked that you didn't back down, Bona!
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_B_021: Naturally. I am a commander of Saramis, after all.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_B_022: Ahhh, what a great fight that was. I remember the\nother soldiers cheering and hollering.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_B_023: We should do it again sometime!
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_B_024: Absolutely not. I am a very busy man.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_B_025: Eh, if you say so. Probably no chance you could beat\nme nowadays.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_B_026: Is that so?
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_B_027: Believe what you will, Tobias. But if we came to\nblows, I would give a good account of myself.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_B_028: That's the spirit, Bona!
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_B_029: I'll clear my schedule. This fight's happening!\nBook it!
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_B_030: Ahaha. Where does he get the energy at his age?
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_A_001: Hah!
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_A_002: Ngaaah!
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_A_003: Phew! You're pretty tough, Bona. Hard to tell which\none of us is winning!
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_A_004: You were a fool to think I had let myself decline. I\nam not called the Mastermind of Saramis for nothing.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_A_005: Oh yeah! From back during the War of Grania.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_A_006: The days when we both fought shoulder to shoulder\nwith King Sergio.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_A_007: Indeed. In hindsight, it was a tumultuous time.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_A_008: All my magic, wisdom, loyalty, and honor was put\nto the test on the battlefield.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_A_009: Yeah. Lotta friends and allies who didn't make it\nout of that one.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_A_010: The empire loved us for keeping the Mosa off\ntheir backs.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_A_011: But their love rang a little hollow.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_A_012: You know... Hehe, somehow, none of us were in a\nworse mood than the princess.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_A_013: "Why didn't you take me along?!" she demanded.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_A_014: All of six years old, and she dressed down the\nadults in the room as if she were queen.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_A_015: Baw haw haw! I remember that! The boss's tantrum\npulled me out of my funk.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_A_016: The "boss," as you were already calling her then,\nhas grown into a proper queen.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_A_017: Listen, Tobias. Neither mind nor might alone are\nsufficient to serve the queen.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_A_018: Both are needed as the situation requires.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_A_019: In other words, the boss needs us both.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_A_020: Correct. Let us continue to serve Her Majesty\ntogether.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_A_021: We shall remain inseparable, Lionheart of Saramis.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_A_022: Hear, hear! You be the boss's right arm, Bona,\nand I'll be the left one!
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_A_023: Er, Tobias...
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_A_024: The "right arm" is a metaphor for one's most trusted\nassociate. The "left arm" means nothing.
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_A_025: Then wouldn't you only have one arm?
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_A_026: A queen of Saramis has gotta have two arms!\nYou know that!
MID_SE_Bon_Tob_A_027: Hmhmhm. A fair point.